      "writtenOn": "2026-07-03T12:47:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "NO,Base Result has 5 fields but worker APIs need only 2 fields to process.\nBy creating a separate, minimal struct for each use case, we keep it independent, eliminate confusing \u0027dead fields[don\u0027t need in collection APIs]\u0027 and make the code much cleaner to maintain.\n\nThe standard, industry-best practice for this situation is, receive the 5-field struct, extract the 2 fields it actually needs, and store them into its own clean 2-field structure to use further.",
