      "writtenOn": "2026-07-06T06:39:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e NO,Base Result has 5 fields but worker APIs need only 2 fields to process.\n\nWhy do you say so? Which tag failed and why is a required information based on which further processing will be done.\nThe use case is not limited to changes brought in by a commit.\n\n\u003e By creating a separate, minimal struct for each use case, we keep it \nindependent, eliminate confusing \u0027dead fields[don\u0027t need in collection \nAPIs]\u0027 and make the code much cleaner to maintain.\n\nBut there is a fine line there, where do you create a balance between code re-usability and independent type based on each use case?\nIn that case what\u0027s you views on having classes defined with multiple members? All the members defined by a class need not be consumed by class(es) instantiating them, should we have separate independent classes with only required members for each use case?\n\n\u003e The standard, industry-best practice for this situation is, receive the \n5-field struct, extract the 2 fields it actually needs, and store them \ninto its own clean 2-field structure to use further.\n\nDo you have a data on that which supports your claim that this is an industry standard?",
